 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity**: Linear with respect to the number of eligible chunks and candidates. MultiMesh creation is O(1) per instance (batched), while Scene instantiation is O(N) where N is scene complexity [G].
-*   **Memory Complexity**: MultiMesh instances are memory-efficient, storing only transform and mesh index. Scene instances consume memory proportional to the scene graph size [G].
+*   **Time Complexity**: Linear with respect to the number of eligible chunks and candidates [G]. MultiMesh creation is O(1) per instance (batched), while Scene instantiation is O(N) where N is scene complexity [G].
+*   **Memory Complexity**: MultiMesh instances are memory-efficient, storing only transform and mesh index [G]. Scene instances consume memory proportional to the scene graph size [G].
 *   **Performance**: MultiMesh is extremely fast and supports collision. Scene instances are slow and should be tuned to low numbers [S1].
 *   **Strengths**: High performance for natural spawning; integrates with terrain LOD; supports persistence [S1].
